     * page where visitors can build and draw maps (#92).
     * Default: assets/home.html.
     * Example override: 'home_page' => __DIR__ . '/home.html',
     */
    'home_page' => __DIR__ . '/../assets/home.html',

    /*
     * Tile providers and their map styles.
     *
     * A request picks a map with `provider` and `style`, for example
     * `provider=carto&style=dark`. With only `provider`, the provider's
     * `default_style` is used; with only `style`, the default provider's style
     * of that name. Unknown, disabled or token-only (without a token) choices
     * get the default map from `defaults.provider` / `defaults.style`.
     *
     * Style ids are shared between providers where they mean the same thing:
     * streets, light, dark, satellite, hybrid (imagery with labels), topo,
     * oceans, and a `-nolabels` suffix for the same style without labels.
     * Provider-specific ids are used only when there is no shared equivalent.
     *
     * Provider keys (all optional except `name` and `styles`):
     *
     *   'name'          (string) Human-readable name of the provider.
     *   'default_style' (string) Style used when a request names this provider
     *                   but no style. Must be one of `styles`. Default: the
     *                   first style.
     *   'styles'        (array, required) The provider's styles, keyed by style
     *                   id. Each style has a `name` (string) and `layers` (list
     *                   of one to five tile URL templates, drawn in order: the
     *                   base map, then e.g. labels on top).
     *                   Placeholders: {z} zoom, {x} column, {y} row, and {key}
     *                   for the API key. {Z}, {X}, {Y} also work. {r} is for
     *                   providers with high-density tiles: it is '@2x' (512 px
     *                   tiles) for scale=2 maps and empty otherwise; without
     *                   it, scale=2 maps use the tiles one zoom level up.
     *   'attribution'   (string) Default attribution, used when the request has
     *                   no `attribution`: 'text' (only the attribution_text),
     *                   a logo ('osm', 'esri', 'mapbox', 'mapbox-small', drawn
     *                   with the text if there is any) or 'none'.
     *                   Falls back to `defaults.attribution`.
     *   'attribution_text' (string) Credit text the provider requires, e.g.
     *                   '© OpenStreetMap contributors'. Drawn on a light strip
     *                   in the attribution corner, wrapped to at most two lines
     *                   (cut short with "…" on small images). Keep it short:
     *                   only what the provider requires on the image.
     *   'attribution_html' (string) The full credit as HTML, with links, for
     *                   clients to show next to the image (for example under a
     *                   map with attribution=none, or for providers that allow
     *                   their full source list near the map instead of on it).
     *                   Served by /api/v1/attribution. Default: the
     *                   attribution_text.
     *   'minzoom'       (int) Lowest zoom served. Default: `zoom.min`.
     *   'maxzoom'       (int) Highest zoom with real tiles (not placeholders).
     *                   Default: `zoom.max`. Capped by `zoom.max_limit` if set.
     *                   The shipped values were checked by sampling tiles in
     *                   several places; the comments say when, and where
     *                   coverage varies by region.
     *   'requires_auth' (bool) Only requests with a valid `token` may use it.
     *                   Default: false.
     *   'enabled'       (bool) Set to false to switch it off on your install.
     *                   Default: true.
     *   'cache'         (string) 'headers' (default): images and tiles may be
     *                   cached as the provider's own HTTP headers allow.
     *                   'off': for providers whose terms forbid caching proxies;
     *                   their map images are sent as private.
     *   'headers'       (array) Request headers sent with every tile request,
     *                   name => value; {key} is replaced with the API key. For
     *                   providers that take the key in a header rather than the
     *                   URL, e.g. ['Authorization' => 'Bearer {key}']. A style
     *                   whose headers use {key} needs a key, like one whose
     *                   URLs do. Tile requests that send headers don't follow
     *                   redirects, so a key is never sent to another server.
     *                   Headers are never shown by the query API.
     *   'bounds'        (array) Area the tiles cover, for regional maps:
     *                   [minLng, minLat, maxLng, maxLat] in degrees. A map
     *                   partly outside gets an `X-Map-Coverage: partial`
     *                   header; one entirely outside gets the default map
     *                   instead (`X-Map-Fallback: outside`). Shown by the
